# C's sql_alert_transitions() with a transition id (`transition=<text>`): C's direct statement, which has no host
# list, no window, no status test and no order. An entry whose statuses are below the window's boundary; two and
# three entries with one transition id, in each order of their global ids (the order C hands them out in is the
# table's); the id's text without hyphens and in capitals; an id no entry has; an entry whose alarm's rule has
# no row of alert_hash; a text that is no UUID (C's record, and no query).
database real
